m-boot Ventoy / Ubuntu exFAT differential experiment

PURPOSE
    Compare m-boot's legacy-BIOS Ubuntu 26.04.1 failure against official
    Ventoy 1.1.18 with identical ISO bytes on exFAT. Do not touch the USB.
    This is experimental and does not yet prove any ISO boot compatibility.

INPUTS
    ventoy-1.1.18-linux.tar.gz
      SHA256 d86ff9de63d94c8b8f1f6b14d23c55af4b88e8207bf2893890892a6a97b1ad54
      https://www.ventoy.net/en/download.html
    ubuntu-26.04.1-desktop-amd64.iso
      SHA256 601e30fbf5d97759367c632e2c33630665039b7e2158fd068403da3ccf1bda1f
      https://releases.ubuntu.com/26.04.1/SHA256SUMS

PREPARE
    Linux x86_64; requires sudo, losetup, lsblk, blkid, mount, partprobe,
    parted, GNU coreutils, tar and enough free space (ISO ~6 GiB).
    Obtain the official Ventoy archive separately, not a git source tree.
    Use the exact operator ISO; a checksum mismatch is a hard failure.

    ./tests/ventoy-ubuntu-exfat.sh prepare \
      --iso /path/to/ubuntu-26.04.1-desktop-amd64.iso \
      --ventoy-tar /path/to/ventoy-1.1.18-linux.tar.gz \
      --output /path/to/existing-disposable-directory

    A NEW private 12 GiB sparse disk image receives Ventoy GPT/exFAT through
    an explicitly verified /dev/loopN device. The script has NO argument
    for selecting any physical block device. The input ISO is copied to
    /m/boot/iso/ and readback-hashed. It prints the resulting raw disk path,
    alongside experiment.txt and results.md. It does not remove the image;
    delete the experiment directory only after preserving results.

NORMAL BOOT
    ./tests/ventoy-ubuntu-exfat.sh boot \
      --disk /path/to/ventoy-ubuntu.XXXXXXXX/ventoy-bios.raw \
      --mode normal

    QEMU parameters: -machine pc -accel tcg -m 2048 -smp 2, BIOS x86_64,
    IDE disk and -snapshot. Select ISO and Normal mode in the Ventoy menu.
    Confirm a genuinely usable Ubuntu live system; splash/BusyBox is FAIL.

GRUB2 BOOT, ONLY AFTER NORMAL FAILURE
    Repeat with --mode grub2; select GRUB2 mode in Ventoy's secondary menu,
    or press Ctrl+r at the main menu before choosing the ISO. Report GRUB2
    separately; it cannot retroactively qualify normal mode as PASS.

EVIDENCE
    Capture firmware/menu and post-kernel state. On success record
    /proc/cmdline, findmnt /, lsblk -f, mount and /dev/mapper contents.
    On failure record BusyBox /proc/cmdline, /proc/filesystems, blkid,
    device-mapper devices and exact errors. Determine whether access to
    the ISO uses a recovered block mapping rather than exFAT mounting.
    Compare against the previously observed m-boot BusyBox failure.
    Never infer general ISO compatibility from one successful example.

BOUNDARIES
    Does not modify any m-boot production menu, ESP, physical USB or
    exFAT partition. Vendor GPLv3+ code is evaluated only as a product
    dependency; do not copy it into m-boot without license review.
